  "notes": "Fighting verse: the command is not glossed; no battle, weapon, march or army drawn; no present-day reading and no people targeted. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. 123:1-11 is not glossed and nothing is drawn in 123 (Al-Muyassar's «ابدؤوا بقتال الأقرب…» is not used); only As-Sa'di's «المعونة من اللّه تنزل بحسب التقوى». 121: the chip starts at «إلا كتب لهم» (a full-verse chip was wider than the screen). Coins for «نفقة», a book for «ليتفقهوا في الدين». STAGING v4: c1 (121) and c3 (123) are kept ambient (spending and crossing valleys on the expedition; the fighting command). c2 (122): a town by day. Both tafsirs say that those who learn are the ones who STAY while a party goes out (Al-Muyassar: «ليتفقه القاعدون عن القتال»; As-Sa'di: «أي: القاعدون»), so three believers sit in the town and nobody is shown going out (no march, no weapon, no army). They read on 122:13 and 122:15 (to gain understanding of the religion: As-Sa'di, to learn the knowledge of the law) under a book plate; three believers (their people, back from going out) walk in from the right on 122:16 (when they return to them) and the believers speak to them on 122:19 (to warn them with what they learned when they return: both tafsirs); nothing is acted on 122:21-22 (that they may beware), the camera is on the people. Nobody faces an empty side and no teacher is implied: the believers read from the book themselves. Cover: the believers reading (122:13)."
